"[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432480} {:answer/id #uuid "7238f33a-029e-5920-a373-cb968bcc10aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432481} {:answer/id #uuid "7960b759-a049-517f-91ce-8f3d3d4ab81c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432482} {:answer/id #uuid "8d5905dd-9d56-563e-ab3a-014628903d88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432484}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432480} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c066721-df4d-58dc-9748-1ef1119a9c18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432494}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1f3bd7e4-e9ee-5ec1-b495-697d442c712e" :question/math-academy-id "q-113070" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=2{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}=-{b}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=2{b}_{1}+{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}=-{b}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. From the second equation, we get \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=-{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=2(-{c}_{2})+{b}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}={c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-{b}_{1}+3{b}_{2} \\\\  & =-(-{c}_{2})+3({c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}) \\\\  & ={c}_{2}+3{c}_{1}+6{c}_{2} \\\\  & =7{c}_{2}+3{c}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].$"} :step/id #uuid "edd9f346-183f-5c36-8e34-bd14bd1d6d98"}] :activity/title "Writing Vectors in Different Bases" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437050}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478491} :activity/id #uuid "b8cd0170-12ba-5a13-8bd5-54a9ef34a08b" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048762 :topic/id #uuid "bc92d9a7-3663-5495-a1b9-4cf735034158" :topic/math-academy-id 1865} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478470 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410062 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20bb3464-f73d-5921-8cdf-f112ab14ead9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410019} {:answer/id #uuid "36299c18-1f12-5691-a4cc-cf600875d435" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410022} {:answer/id #uuid "7f7a28ee-dddd-5aff-9301-8500542e8d7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410031} {:answer/id #uuid "d1ea2e8b-285d-5d4a-86b6-3118e3eacc94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410041} {:answer/id #uuid "e5b40102-f333-5f07-9467-4d1fb5ba690a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410046}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410019} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8e25391-7c4e-5c7c-8ae1-5b47ead04007" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410055}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f46f0e34-3d5c-5e7a-9fb4-690993802dbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-81230" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}={b}_{1}+{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}={b}_{2}-{b}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}={b}_{1}+{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}={b}_{2}-{b}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. By adding the equations, we get \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}=2{b}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}={b}_{1}+(\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2})\\,⟹\\,{b}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =7{b}_{1}+{b}_{2} \\\\  & =7(\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2})+(\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}{c}_{1}-\\frac{7}{2}{c}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2} \\\\  & =4{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$"} :step/id #uuid "06723a52-a509-54e8-a958-1ee3d11c3842" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478483}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478475 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247309 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18b734f7-2e56-5969-b91b-fd5d7834144a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244533} {:answer/id #uuid "55d5c155-aa97-5099-976e-267010b9f696" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245069} {:answer/id #uuid "7fbe273e-6df1-5251-8f0b-69494a5c2141" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245440} {:answer/id #uuid "8a957706-ca6f-56cc-883e-020725d0d396" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245527} {:answer/id #uuid "b92afccc-c74b-5377-acc9-db0f72855208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245967}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245967} :answer-field/id #uuid "e597727d-4abc-5787-967c-bd4759284ec9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246957}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9c8b3d18-f99b-57ac-806c-9402fb0d526b" :question/math-academy-id "q-112855" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=2{b}_{1}+3{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}={b}_{1}+2{b}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=2{b}_{1}+3{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}={b}_{1}+2{b}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. Multiplying the second equation by $-2$ and adding the equations, we get  \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}-2{c}_{2}=-{b}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}=-{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{c}_{2}={b}_{1}+2(-{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2})\\,⟹\\,{b}_{1}=2{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{b}_{1}-3{b}_{2} \\\\  & =2(2{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2})-3(-{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}) \\\\  & =4{c}_{1}-6{c}_{2}+3{c}_{1}-6{c}_{2} \\\\  & =7{c}_{1}-12{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].$"} :step/id #uuid "374bc840-79bd-5b15-a6b4-c10eeb6fda83"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478481 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410061 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4acab282-04ec-5eb0-ae3a-7ab839526ee4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410024} {:answer/id #uuid "ad9fccc8-89c8-5084-95ed-898b492b9317" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410037} {:answer/id #uuid "af3b103c-e7ac-56f6-8025-6eee882f5637" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410038} {:answer/id #uuid "f26fb59e-92cb-5f2d-bb4b-31538da03416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410047} {:answer/id #uuid "f9547433-2214-505b-b38c-379846b86b1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410049}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410049} :answer-field/id #uuid "66650074-ff68-5eca-a6ce-c53f9965f0b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c92100bd-871b-5993-bed2-e255a4c7bcbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-35246" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=-2{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}=-3{b}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5{b}_{1}-2{b}_{2} \\\\  & =-2{b}_{2}+5{b}_{1} \\\\  & =-2{b}_{2}-\\frac{5}{3}(-3{b}_{1}) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}-\\frac{5}{3}{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}].$"} :step/id #uuid "7fbd79a1-9017-5962-8464-c8335e25c404" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478470}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478483 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247306 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43596b54-0af5-56a0-a954-2be5f40712fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244900} {:answer/id #uuid "8b479d14-ade5-5b29-9efe-2745148ba46e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245536} {:answer/id #uuid "be780025-c235-58a6-8299-86b26eaeee98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246012} {:answer/id #uuid "e089e494-fe55-562d-9268-21868311ca66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246310} {:answer/id #uuid "e8c12ab0-ecc5-5590-8676-6569049bf30f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246374}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245536} :answer-field/id #uuid "03d089c3-601c-50be-8dc4-891bcf11d265" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246555}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f5c48c40-2fd0-5515-867f-1f3be83f3dfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-112656" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=4{b}_{3}$, ${c}_{2}=2{b}_{1}$ and ${c}_{3}=\\frac{1}{2}{b}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{b}_{1}+2{b}_{2}+8{b}_{3} \\\\  & =8{b}_{3}+2{b}_{1}+2{b}_{2} \\\\  & =2(4{b}_{3})+2{b}_{1}+2\\cdot 2(\\frac{1}{2}{b}_{2}) \\\\  & =2{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+4{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$"} :step/id #uuid "9647de70-ff9d-5f4b-bc4e-14a190bb842f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478475}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478491 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120362 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "252cd9d2-cd28-51d0-86dc-f100bfbf8425" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410020} {:answer/id #uuid "65ce31d1-a577-5b44-a7fa-3c3f399d7aa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 6 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410028} {:answer/id #uuid "b63f4cd2-57fd-5205-92b4-a5bf14cc8ff8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ 6 \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410040} {:answer/id #uuid "e15510ae-a912-51f2-b92f-d981d02b25f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410045} {:answer/id #uuid "fe8e8b08-4548-5fe8-adbd-3bce3207c85e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 6 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410050}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410028} :answer-field/id #uuid "de484491-607f-5712-bf20-9fe92c23a765" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410057}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "59ed1787-672a-57bb-b86d-43224b917d2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-34772" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=3{b}_{2}$, ${c}_{2}=-{b}_{3}$ and ${c}_{3}=4{b}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-3{b}_{1}+4{b}_{2}-6{b}_{3} \\\\  & =4{b}_{2}-6{b}_{3}-3{b}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}(3{b}_{2})+6(-{b}_{3})-\\frac{3}{4}(4{b}_{1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{c}_{1}+6{c}_{2}-\\frac{3}{4}{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 6 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}].$"} :step/id #uuid "c6f946eb-8d53-5f69-9732-0e531c296bb0" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478481}}] :activity/title "Writing Vectors in Different Bases" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477731}] [{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134901} :activity/id #uuid "fc007430-4cc9-562b-9192-4d3c9dccd500" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049312 :topic/id #uuid "eb826c2f-ae04-5de5-b6a6-7efcf7e974ae" :topic/math-academy-id 2201} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134901 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135151 :tutorial/content "If an $n\\!\\times \\!n$ matrix $A$ has an entire row or column of zeros, then its determinant is equal to zero.\n\nFor example, consider the matrix $A$ given below:\n\n![](images/6b/6bb8b64f7ed8730e641cdf88fc6fe7add40bc15061095c6b1f57c1b764b28feb.svg)\n\nThe second row consists of all zeros, and the asterisks ($\\ast$) may represent any number.\n\nLet's compute the determinant using the Laplace expansion across the second row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)^{2+1}(0)|\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}|+(-1)^{2+2}(0)|\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}|+(-1)^{2+3}(0)|\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0+0+0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that it doesn't matter what numbers are represented by the asterisks ($\\ast$). Each cofactor is multiplied by zero, so the final result must be zero." :tutorial/id #uuid "cee0a552-60f2-5785-a506-63bd053364c7" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6888 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "b68428f5-f5bb-5090-b7f9-4971dc931914" :step/math-academy-id 41745 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134902}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134902 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135152 :tutorial/content "Now, suppose a matrix has no zero rows but it has two identical rows:\n\n![](images/74/7477781b618ec384b1638d01707acf545e7d9882ffca5bbc0efde4e224b04308.svg)\n\nWe can subtract the $1$st row from the $3$rd row, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this operation does not change the determinant, we get $\\det(A) = \\det(B).$ Furthermore, as $B$ contains a zero row, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\det(A) = \\det(B) = 0.\n$$\n\nNotice that we can use this method with columns too. Therefore, we have the following property:\n\n*If a square matrix has at least two identical rows/columns, its determinant equals zero.*" :tutorial/id #uuid "6813d49e-3908-5735-8196-8e1aad5a14e6" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6889 :tutorial/title "Determinants with Identical Rows or Identical Columns"} :step/id #uuid "e105e6ae-64b8-5812-85e8-b5c3ef7b6c7d" :step/math-academy-id 41746 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134903}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134903 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133911 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133466 :question/id #uuid "bb2795c3-6359-50d8-9531-1e9dfae7a2ce" :question/math-academy-id "e-10994"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "28142e26-f6c7-54c9-9c16-035c75f7659f" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048462} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049159}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134395} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134408} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272009} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329700} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351408} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400867} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420351} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420352} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427636} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484213} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484278}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With A Zero Row/Column or Two Identical Rows/Columns"} :step/id #uuid "f2a27f52-c605-5d01-84c1-49531f59d922" :step/math-academy-id 41747 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134904}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134904 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135153 :tutorial/content "Now, suppose a matrix has no zero rows and no identical rows but it has two proportional rows:\n\n![](images/81/8181d36ff1378310744b0d74f42f2934eb1e41053f45ecfeacf0c813abe994df.svg)\n\nWe can add three times the $1$st row to the $3$rd row, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -6 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this operation does not change the determinant, we get $\\det(A) = \\det(B).$ Furthermore, as $B$ contains a zero row, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\det(A) = \\det(B) = 0.\n$$\n\nNotice that we can use this method with columns too. Therefore, we have the following property:\n\n*If a square matrix has at least two proportional rows/columns, its determinant equals zero.*" :tutorial/id #uuid "fe83e8c9-948a-596f-a2d9-c2ae2fe4f335" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6890 :tutorial/title "Determinants with Proportional Rows/Columns"} :step/id #uuid "23e26677-bdeb-5a45-a6d3-4a8d02a72732" :step/math-academy-id 41750 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134905}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134905 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133912 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133467 :question/id #uuid "dc780837-b763-5ba9-981a-2373afcb524a" :question/math-academy-id "e-10995"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aef330a-81b3-56c4-9559-67df673e8687" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134394} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134407} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272011} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329654} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351409} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402861} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402868} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411852} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415475} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415477} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415478} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484193}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Two Proportional Rows/Columns"} :step/id #uuid "93111f5e-5fd2-5a5b-81b1-27969a9b5d1d" :step/math-academy-id 41751 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134906}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134906 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135154 :tutorial/content "In conclusion, if an $n\\!\\times \\!n$ matrix $A$ satisfies any one of the following conditions, then $\\det(A)=0.$\n\nI. $A$ has a zero row/column\n\nII. $A$ has two identical rows/columns\n\nIII. $A$ has two proportional rows/columns\n\nIV. $A$ has a row/column that is a linear combination of other rows/columns\n\nNotice that condition IV encompasses each of the conditions I, II, and III. If we have a zero row/column, two identical rows/columns, or proportional rows/columns, then the rows/columns form a linearly dependent set of vectors. \nIn turn, this means that one of the rows/columns is a linear combination of other rows/columns.\n\n**Watch out!** While all of the above conditions are *sufficient* to conclude that $\\det(A)=0,$ only condition IV is *necessary* to conclude that $\\det(A)=0.$ \nIn other words, if we have a matrix $A$ with $\\det(A)=0,$ then conditions I, II, and III may or may not be satisfied, while condition IV *must* be satisfied. \n\nSo, we have the following theorem:\n\n*$\\det(A)=0$ if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nFinally, note also that in the case of a $2\\times 2$ matrix *only*, statements III and IV mean the same thing." :tutorial/id #uuid "9d8b0323-170c-5a60-b372-1a258c4848cc" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6891 :tutorial/title "Conditions When a Determinant Equals Zero"} :step/id #uuid "4aec093b-050b-5263-9ef2-c875455b8c07" :step/math-academy-id 41754 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134908}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134907 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133913 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133468 :question/id #uuid "33ca37e5-c598-52a2-861f-2d5bfa6fd571" :question/math-academy-id "e-10996"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134393} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134414} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272012} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272013} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329652} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329653} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329699} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351410} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415476} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415479} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420353}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"} :step/id #uuid "81571aa7-ce3d-5713-bf67-a49538fee0ef" :step/math-academy-id 41755} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134908 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135155 :tutorial/content "Geometrically, the absolute value of an $n \\times n$ determinant can be interpreted as the volume of the $n$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the columns of the determinant. \n\nFor example:\n\n- Suppose the columns of a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ are ${\\color{black}\\mathbf{a}}, {\\color{black}\\mathbf{b}},$ and ${\\color{black}\\mathbf{c}}.$\n![](images/6e/6e046341b7a1b8f6760797f7db89a7e021a6ace6b5cdf28bd5217998cb450837.svg)\nThe $3$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the columns of $A$ is depicted below:\n\n![](images/25/2597b48a010607fca71c551dbce8e9e2bbeda47d0892a582347ae1cdf19f1bf6.png)\n\nThe volume $V$ of this parallelepiped equals the absolute value of the determinant of $A{:}$\n\n$$\nV = \\left|\\det(A)\\right|\n$$\n\n- Now suppose the columns of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $B$ are ${\\color{black}\\mathbf{p}}$ and ${\\color{black}\\mathbf{q}}.$\n![](images/f5/f593c123eb081da0399e74c665325774758b48c5f086a7475b959905e1de2763.svg)\nThe $2$-dimensional parallelepiped (i.e., the parallelogram) spanned by vectors $\\mathbf{p}$ and $\\mathbf{q}$ is shown below:\n\n![](images/4a/4af1971404b188df75bb3d62d47ac95340c5e1791066e5358370d743230baa45.png)\n\nThe two-dimensional volume $V$ (i.e., the area) of this parallelepiped equals the absolute value of the determinant of $B{:}$\n\n$$\nV = \\left|\\det(B)\\right|\n$$\n\n- In general, the absolute value of the determinant of an $n\\times n$ matrix $M$ gives the $n$-dimensional volume of the parallelepiped spanned by the columns of $M.$\n\nIn this lesson, we studied the following property:\n\n*$\\det(A) = 0$ if and only if one of the columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other columns of $A$.*\n\nWhat does this property mean in geometric terms?\n\nThe component $\\det(A) = 0$ implies that the $n$-dimensional parallelepiped formed by the columns of $A$ has zero volume. Conversely, when one of the columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other columns, it indicates that the corresponding parallelepiped possesses at most $n-1$ distinct dimensions. \n\nConsider the following examples:\n\n- In the case of a $3$-dimensional parallelepiped, if the vector $\\mathbf{c}$ is a linear combination of the vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$, then $\\mathbf{c}$ lies within the plane containing $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$. In other words, the vectors $\\mathbf{a}$, $\\mathbf{b}$, and $\\mathbf{c}$ are coplanar. Consequently, we obtain a \"flat\" ($2$-dimensional) figure with a volume of $0$.\n\n- For the parallelogram example, if the vector $\\mathbf{q}$ is a linear combination of the vector $\\mathbf{p}$ (i.e., $\\mathbf{p}$ and $\\mathbf{q}$ are proportional), then $\\mathbf{q}$ resides on the line containing vector $\\mathbf{p}$. In other words, the vectors $\\mathbf{p}$ and $\\mathbf{q}$ are collinear. This results in a $1$-dimensional object with a $2$-dimensional volume (i.e., area) of $0$." :tutorial/id #uuid "1f7191c6-60ca-5c44-befc-8dbad7779b08" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6893 :tutorial/title "Geometric Interpretation of a Zero Determinant"} :step/id #uuid "8c5dbeea-b2e4-5fe9-9d8c-98750164b70c" :step/math-academy-id 41766 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134907}}] :activity/title "Conditions When a Determinant Equals Zero" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186134042}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046673} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415480} :activity/id #uuid "d3285aa6-5f09-548a-886c-a1acc2f7b8d6" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049312 :topic/id #uuid "eb826c2f-ae04-5de5-b6a6-7efcf7e974ae" :topic/math-academy-id 2201} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415480 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415477 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "022ff781-0bb6-5222-8917-bb9fe088d40f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415445} {:answer/id #uuid "68acb0f6-b335-5e47-b870-8fcc301ed02a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415455} {:answer/id #uuid "a31adf10-60d1-51b5-9022-8cf1940c42be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415461} {:answer/id #uuid "ebaffa84-7e8a-5edc-8432-6adf9e5b2b42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415465} {:answer/id #uuid "fae22a7a-c8b8-5a0b-bb2c-5bc815b3b48d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415467}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415445} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9ec239f-8a57-5ead-b4ff-042aa539477e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d4554f29-f5fb-5556-852c-2f9d95422a4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-42464" :question/problem "Find $5det(A)+7det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{2} & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has proportional rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has a zero column, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{2} & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $5det(A)+7det(B)=5\\cdot 0+7\\cdot 0=0.$"} :step/id #uuid "0922e6fb-1dc5-5a88-a985-bdf2643cb465" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415484}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415481 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415479 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c54ada56-3e8b-562f-84dd-634b27dac9cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453904} {:answer/id #uuid "1bc835ea-e9b6-5ca5-a77e-0c3bd1af050b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453905}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453904} :answer-field/id #uuid "63c0a961-3dd4-5dcd-85e3-43b3a0493c55" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454702} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2456bbca-5dde-5fa3-a774-4b5dfb8431ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453906} {:answer/id #uuid "1b80c1f5-4c11-5a34-bb1a-faf5cdfce42f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453907}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453906} :answer-field/id #uuid "36456e08-b5e0-5ffb-8bc0-2e13784267ad" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454703} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e336f47-61c7-5dfa-b071-bc593d519e33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453908} {:answer/id #uuid "05d59b93-9de5-5bdc-af50-0154b6214595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453909}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453909} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bb3bd4f-a1b2-5b23-a316-a0c1d1cd0bc3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454704}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f8a11ae3-b740-5975-a251-a4796d69b742" :question/math-academy-id "q-43307" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $3\\times 3$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ has a zero column\n- **II.** $A$ has two proportional rows\n- **III.** One of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nExpending across the $1$st column, we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3-2)+(1-2) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut $A$ has neither a zero column nor two proportional rows.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} :step/id #uuid "73a434b3-1e72-5102-a3b4-f3e485e5088a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415482}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415482 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415475 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "045918a8-9cd8-5a07-b550-ae46024d9091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415446} {:answer/id #uuid "402ee237-56af-5ed0-b68b-15a4eb93a4c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415451} {:answer/id #uuid "82c9a685-f3be-5652-9e92-444a23e21632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415458} {:answer/id #uuid "f5705fa2-288d-561a-9ae0-435e05884593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|,$ $|B|,$ and $|C|$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415466} {:answer/id #uuid "fff98d8e-e1e9-59ce-9f45-62d4096f2b19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415469}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415466} :answer-field/id #uuid "3898e8c8-305f-5107-8e55-3fa0057b225c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415470}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "135c5d03-e391-5a5b-8227-7d54c7203318" :question/math-academy-id "q-140048" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 2 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a triangular matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n|A|=0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0=0\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has proportional rows: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 2 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, $|A|,$ $|B|,$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$"} :step/id #uuid "7fde0eea-1a95-5e36-bc1d-53171442da99"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415483 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415478 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1859d7c5-0d55-5273-a004-f8368886466b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415448} {:answer/id #uuid "4a61a420-d52d-5f1a-b48b-ade03dffdca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415453} {:answer/id #uuid "5fcc61bd-b9ee-5f9e-8558-651f8ea9c858" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415454} {:answer/id #uuid "851dc3ec-467b-568b-a964-3b5e34b3527e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415459} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e4e722-717d-508c-a98d-112f70b09d9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415463}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415463} :answer-field/id #uuid "f920ea7f-06a7-52e9-8586-d0e6b44af6b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415474}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e897ce2c-45dd-5cf3-9d25-ca84c0dd6ea8" :question/math-academy-id "q-42881" :question/problem "Find $3det(A)-det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0.57 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a triangular matrix, we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=2\\cdot 1\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has proportional columns, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0.57 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $3det(A)-det(B)=3\\cdot 6-0=18.$"} :step/id #uuid "8a73fe86-1dcc-5158-b5d0-cfa5bf0ca01e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415481}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415484 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415476 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "071ee791-8aa1-59a9-829e-f23787b55570" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473130} {:answer/id #uuid "be789ad4-7b1c-517c-b647-7e02fbdc4606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473131}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186473131} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c846e82-5642-55c2-bd6c-bf9a65cc14b7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473960} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "380f5ebb-1b0a-524b-8107-7d50c50a8d0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473132} {:answer/id #uuid "2adc7349-dd06-5e86-bb35-5bbbb5b04583" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473133}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186473132} :answer-field/id #uuid "37aa9389-4822-5c22-ad9b-bf758d46df45" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473961} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2322edf-ee14-5f20-8831-ec7cadfc1dd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473134} {:answer/id #uuid "d8ca5be3-1fbc-5f41-bcbb-41b53ef5da56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473135}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186473135} :answer-field/id #uuid "873d7824-ac7f-5ce0-ad45-49263a39fd15" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473962}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8d883981-f066-5218-a1bf-dd76574de46e" :question/math-academy-id "q-42469" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n- **I.** $A$ has proportional columns\n- **II.** $A$ has identical rows\n- **III.** $A$ has a zero row\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\n- $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "a995ede1-d1f3-53d5-97cb-aed29dce50f7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415483}}] :activity/title "Conditions When a Determinant Equals Zero" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415444}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416116} :activity/id #uuid "9cb6054b-7ed5-5992-92b3-318764a5074c" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049312 :topic/id #uuid "eb826c2f-ae04-5de5-b6a6-7efcf7e974ae" :topic/math-academy-id 2201} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416114 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415477 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "022ff781-0bb6-5222-8917-bb9fe088d40f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415445} {:answer/id #uuid "68acb0f6-b335-5e47-b870-8fcc301ed02a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415455} {:answer/id #uuid "a31adf10-60d1-51b5-9022-8cf1940c42be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415461} {:answer/id #uuid "ebaffa84-7e8a-5edc-8432-6adf9e5b2b42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415465} {:answer/id #uuid "fae22a7a-c8b8-5a0b-bb2c-5bc815b3b48d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415467}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415445} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9ec239f-8a57-5ead-b4ff-042aa539477e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d4554f29-f5fb-5556-852c-2f9d95422a4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-42464" :question/problem "Find $5det(A)+7det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{2} & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has proportional rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has a zero column, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{2} & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $5det(A)+7det(B)=5\\cdot 0+7\\cdot 0=0.$"} :step/id #uuid "21677cec-5329-5c17-ae68-e4ce9c1eced7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416118}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416115 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272012 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "643b4a3a-7263-51ad-8b17-fdd82678cf99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464084} {:answer/id #uuid "e3e66fb8-1a18-56f4-8033-3baba4940db9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464085}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186464084} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ceb200f-e369-571b-b619-8f16a603488c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464976} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "198009c8-d9e6-556e-aa1c-228a37b12311" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464086} {:answer/id #uuid "da19cf9c-0b56-5a20-b004-c70d313f5184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464087}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186464087} :answer-field/id #uuid "d98905ac-4493-5551-96b2-6d52f8e3f566" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464977} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63ea76cf-d936-573e-a0be-56de7954b8ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464088} {:answer/id #uuid "24e2aa19-faca-5a81-a238-e9e984e89ef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464089}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186464089} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed42e6d2-1aff-5708-ad8c-b45de0195450" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464978}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f60fdb9d-cf89-59bd-ad65-e9ec096b82df" :question/math-academy-id "q-140049" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $|A|\\ne 0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n- **I.** $A$ is a triangular matrix\n- **II.** $A$ does not have identical rows\n- **III.** $A$ does not have proportional columns\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have that \n\n$$\n|A|=1\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 2=5\\ne 0\n$$\n\nbut $A$ is not a triangular matrix.\n\n- Statements II and III are true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nIn the case of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, this means that one of the rows/columns must be proportional to another row/column.\nHence, if $|A|\\ne 0$ then $A$ doesn't have proportional nor identical rows/columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."} :step/id #uuid "5d4a636e-e59e-599e-aff6-d3384708bbf3"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416116 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329652 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ecd3639-37c9-5252-aa12-89458787a945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467506} {:answer/id #uuid "4a17d94f-af1d-51db-b4a1-c3f5d3f929bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467507}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467506} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdf24f07-c421-5ff2-bb73-41cf2a1bb824" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468474} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6ede3e0-89dd-5960-bddd-720db62f0e98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467508} {:answer/id #uuid "9298449a-ad9c-56e2-ac99-09c0dc4fccc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467509}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467509} :answer-field/id #uuid "c910b60c-d032-56a5-9324-9976088368c8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468475} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b966358-ec55-5272-a99d-1379768d11ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467510} {:answer/id #uuid "7421f4b3-99e2-5360-a4df-4fcdc8cb3bc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467511}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467511} :answer-field/id #uuid "5de5adf3-aa9f-52a9-9f7f-305d17cf782d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468476}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fffc6699-6d6e-50bb-8cc3-7d4f0e3f1d17" :question/math-academy-id "q-42460" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n- **I.** $A$ has a zero row\n- **II.** $A$ has two proportional columns\n- **III.** $A$ has two identical rows\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have a zero row.\n\n- $A$ has two proportional columns:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ has two identical rows: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "72236d0c-8f54-552b-be75-f74f2ec50cbd" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416114}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416117 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415479 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c54ada56-3e8b-562f-84dd-634b27dac9cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453904} {:answer/id #uuid "1bc835ea-e9b6-5ca5-a77e-0c3bd1af050b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453905}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453904} :answer-field/id #uuid "63c0a961-3dd4-5dcd-85e3-43b3a0493c55" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454702} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2456bbca-5dde-5fa3-a774-4b5dfb8431ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453906} {:answer/id #uuid "1b80c1f5-4c11-5a34-bb1a-faf5cdfce42f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453907}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453906} :answer-field/id #uuid "36456e08-b5e0-5ffb-8bc0-2e13784267ad" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454703} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e336f47-61c7-5dfa-b071-bc593d519e33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453908} {:answer/id #uuid "05d59b93-9de5-5bdc-af50-0154b6214595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453909}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453909} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bb3bd4f-a1b2-5b23-a316-a0c1d1cd0bc3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454704}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f8a11ae3-b740-5975-a251-a4796d69b742" :question/math-academy-id "q-43307" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $3\\times 3$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ has a zero column\n- **II.** $A$ has two proportional rows\n- **III.** One of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nExpending across the $1$st column, we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3-2)+(1-2) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut $A$ has neither a zero column nor two proportional rows.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} :step/id #uuid "cd1aa3f6-63e2-5747-ab7a-9aca6a4ae1ae" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416115}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416118 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402861 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78b84216-c188-5769-a0cf-2f3c4b5d4fe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402863} {:answer/id #uuid "47a2ba38-2156-5dd9-922d-70e7a9112796" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402864} {:answer/id #uuid "bf232768-62b0-5a99-b6ae-c2f1d1ac4e96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402865} {:answer/id #uuid "5c171a58-43ca-5ac8-896f-be2e38df60c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402866} {:answer/id #uuid "75bb085b-9153-5df0-9e32-3ce23b5de8fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402867}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402863} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4619bd4-0fd6-5b0e-85d8-4d713cc4997e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402862}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b44f28c6-ca93-5246-be2b-1a2725d36e07" :question/math-academy-id "q-43057" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & -6 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 8 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2\\sqrt{2} & 8 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is a triangular matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|A|=3\\cdot (-6)\\cdot 2=-36\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has proportional rows: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2\\sqrt{2} & 8 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is a triangular matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|C|=(-1)\\cdot 3\\cdot 4=-12\\ne 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $|B|$ is equal to $0.$"} :step/id #uuid "dd405466-fc10-5821-904a-fe28c7027da8" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416117}}] :activity/title "Conditions When a Determinant Equals Zero" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416113}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427638} :activity/id #uuid "831bdc32-0d6c-55b8-aa0e-17d1809789f3" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049312 :topic/id #uuid "eb826c2f-ae04-5de5-b6a6-7efcf7e974ae" :topic/math-academy-id 2201} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427637 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415475 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "045918a8-9cd8-5a07-b550-ae46024d9091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415446} {:answer/id #uuid "402ee237-56af-5ed0-b68b-15a4eb93a4c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415451} {:answer/id #uuid "82c9a685-f3be-5652-9e92-444a23e21632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415458} {:answer/id #uuid "f5705fa2-288d-561a-9ae0-435e05884593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|,$ $|B|,$ and $|C|$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415466} {:answer/id #uuid "fff98d8e-e1e9-59ce-9f45-62d4096f2b19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415469}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415466} :answer-field/id #uuid "3898e8c8-305f-5107-8e55-3fa0057b225c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415470}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "135c5d03-e391-5a5b-8227-7d54c7203318" :question/math-academy-id "q-140048" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 2 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a triangular matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n|A|=0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0=0\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has proportional rows: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 2 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, $|A|,$ $|B|,$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$"} :step/id #uuid "1a88a749-d24f-53f0-b27d-bb6b30fd5b09"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427638 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329653 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7a447b8-7f09-5270-aca4-b17f9770d76a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467512} {:answer/id #uuid "20bcc14b-7336-54e8-a261-0dbcc7509b69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467513}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467513} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b661764-dcf8-5eba-bedc-e2374ffb5a83" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468477} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f27d7c7-943c-56e2-9e1a-eb7154c900ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467514} {:answer/id #uuid "9113697f-b704-5925-b69c-e204a21d502a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467515}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467514} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba64ddd8-bbc6-577f-b73b-e524ed587e49" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468478} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68448d61-0ddf-531f-8009-f672e592a9b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467516} {:answer/id #uuid "84b46424-4893-5f87-bbc8-ae085db91a24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467517}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467516} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2a724bd-e000-5d5f-b930-fed8c566efc4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468479}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "59d4edee-acd9-59e0-80f8-ec390e2e0ee0" :question/math-academy-id "q-42465" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & \\sqrt{6} & 9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 4 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\nI. $A$ has proportional rows\n\nII. $A$ has identical columns\n\nIII. $A$ has a zero column\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has proportional rows: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & \\sqrt{6} & 9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 4 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have a zero column.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} :step/id #uuid "388fa099-949a-55ed-903a-cb5e3105da1f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427639}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427639 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134407 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba7d7bc9-77ef-583c-8caa-22315aad7aca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$, $|B|$, and $|C|$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392523} {:answer/id #uuid "23f02ed7-eb83-5988-a1ca-ee80eac659ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392524} {:answer/id #uuid "d767aec8-a44c-5175-bbcd-b71f577015fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392525} {:answer/id #uuid "ee7ae539-44fc-5d03-b8b9-5a5b498db62e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392526} {:answer/id #uuid "3737a2a5-a57d-571a-a651-f2cad4ee3049" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392527}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392525} :answer-field/id #uuid "00ef10bc-f305-5726-8271-949923025e38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cee2c526-7176-535a-81f7-173bfaefecec" :question/math-academy-id "q-42882" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{2} & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{2} & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a triangular matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|B|=1\\cdot 3\\cdot 4=12\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$"} :step/id #uuid "38a574a5-5c5f-57c3-888b-5d032802d120" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427640}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427640 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134414 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cc3eb36-fa25-5b0c-a9f4-d0d9b6fd431c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448644} {:answer/id #uuid "024de02f-c585-5ff1-ae1f-906a7964b6c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448645}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448644} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4ba6b54-8b9e-5c38-a842-718279128c22" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449362} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8759331-0ea5-5e82-a056-c79e5438af33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448646} {:answer/id #uuid "e2f5cff8-7a78-538b-955f-a82c9351731b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448647}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448647} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae83d106-f07c-5d04-9fd2-5832bd202f49" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449363} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "318ceaba-c9a3-5098-81fd-4d438f7912e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448648} {:answer/id #uuid "773df97a-4a06-5ac8-b5d2-9731cc8bba08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448649}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448648} :answer-field/id #uuid "93e5158f-ae92-576e-abfb-6ad450c72c06" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449364}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ef67ff18-5c70-5c00-bdf0-27b79dc90b72" :question/math-academy-id "q-43306" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ has two identical rows\n\n- **II.** One of the rows/columns of $A$ is proportional to another row/column of $A$\n\n- **III.** $A$ has two identical columns" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statements I and III are false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have that \n\n$$\n|A|=1\\cdot 8-4\\cdot 2=0\n$$\n\nbut $A$ has neither two identical rows nor two identical columns.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nIn the case of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, this means that one of the rows/columns must be proportional to another row/column.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."} :step/id #uuid "9758fa31-2a83-569c-bfa7-a2c551b1e63f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427641}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427641 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427636 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c03a16b-9dee-5cff-a0ff-6bb3df36fd82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427630} {:answer/id #uuid "317dd47a-723e-5f7b-bb84-76a98d476a7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427631} {:answer/id #uuid "51f27d1e-2a2e-57fb-a28c-b54b35283c0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427632} {:answer/id #uuid "a64fab7a-ae4b-5ae6-9ea8-75c59aee1472" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427633} {:answer/id #uuid "c7ae2b06-54e1-5537-a7a1-e4af212bb060" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427634}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427630} :answer-field/id #uuid "25bbbab1-f79f-5a4a-95b4-1d90cbb77585" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427635}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "df55035e-2530-507b-9e8e-793ed8f0bafc" :question/math-academy-id "q-82284" :question/problem "Find $-4det(A)+3det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{2} & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has a zero column, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ is a triangular matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal: \n\n$$\ndet(B)=\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot 3=6\n$$\n\nTherefore, $-4det(A)+3det(B)=-4\\cdot 0+3\\cdot 6=18.$"} :step/id #uuid "f880731a-4b09-56ca-8e32-d2d537e03030" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427637}}] :activity/title "Conditions When a Determinant Equals Zero" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427629}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499619} :activity/id #uuid "7116892c-7fc3-5b1b-aa93-d2dfc9d1e89e" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049312 :to